WEBVTT

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.040
<i>At any rate, I was hungry.</i>

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.980
<i>A lone high school student, 
hungry at this hour.</i>

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:14.520
<i>Pathetic.</i>

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.950
Tempura Mermaid

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.300
<i>Oh? Tempura...</i>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.300
<i>That might be good.</i>

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:22.560
Welcome!

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.640
<i>I see. Mermaid was indeed apt.</i>

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.940
What'll you have?

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:36.090
<b>Shrimp Tempura Meal
Scallop Tempura Meal 
Dolphin Tempura Meal 
Mermaid Tempura Meal 
Vegetable Tempura Meal</b>

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.840
<i>Dolphin tempura meal? Is that even okay?</i>

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.570
<i>But I have to try this.</i>

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:36.090
The mermaid meal.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.560
<b>Mermaid Meal</b>

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:44.020
<b>Beer
It's non-alcoholic beer, 
so even minors can drink it!</b>

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:48.480
<b>Mystery Side Dish
Can't say what meat is in it.
S-- Sheph--d might 
have a problem with it.</b>

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:54.700
I taste great with beer!

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.770
It was a dream.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.370
<i>Why did I dream about human tempura?</i>

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.870
<i>Kirihito Sanka?!</i>

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.230
Prepare to operate!

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:08.110
Achzion-br---e!

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:20.540
<b>Muromi-san on the Shore</b>

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:20.540
<b>Episode 10
"Muromi-san Worldwide"</b>

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.200
This is pretty!

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.930
Hey you, girl...

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.610
Could you get me some 
water or something?

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:00.640
What's wrong?

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.090
Are you feeling sick?

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.070
I drank a little too much last night—

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:14.500
Here you go.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.840
It's not water, but will this do?

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.200
Coconut?

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.390
Thanks. This'll be fine.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:21.220
Wait just a second.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.470
I'll get something to cut it open with.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:23.610
It's fine.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.640
I've got it.

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:40.740
I think I feel a bit better now.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:43.100
Thanks for that.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.940
If I could repay you somehow...

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.700
Hold on a second.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:50.650
<b>Incoming Call
 Sumida</b>

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.650
Hello.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.030
Oh, Sumida-san?

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:56.370
Yo, what's up?

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.080
What? A mixer?

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.180
When? Where? Who's coming?

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.860
Tonight? The Baltic Sea?

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:02.850
Could you hold on a sec?

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.040
Sorry, where are we?

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:04.970
Malaysia.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.600
The opposite side of the continent.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:12.420
<b>Current 
Location</b>

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.180
<b>Destination</b>

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:12.050
Whether I go north or south, it'd 
take half a day to make it there.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.420
<b>Destination</b>

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.900
So who's going to be there?

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.170
What? The kraken?

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.530
I don't like him.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.150
We'll need another girl?

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.500
Yeah, totally.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.040
He can't handle his liquor.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:28.370
The other day, he was trying to 
show off in front of some girls,

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:31.290
and he tried to take out 
this Russian nuclear sub.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:36.830
If we didn't stop him, we could have 
been looking at World War III.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:38.550
Yeah, I know, right?

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:42.550
It's like he doesn't get why he 
isn't popular with the ladies.

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:48.020
I get you owe him one, but 
I'm hung over right now.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.910
Can't Levia-san head over there?

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.020
I'm sure if she's there,

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.160
the kraken won't make as much as a peep.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.100
I see, so she can't come 
'cause she's on vacation.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.650
How about this, then?

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.940
We'll get him smashed first.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.880
We fire off some compliments 
and get him feeling good.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.560
Then we leave him and have 
him take care of the bill.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:08.370
We take off and drink at another place.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.950
I say we head up the Seine 
and go to Burgundy.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.160
Sound good?

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:16.000
Anyway, tell everyone 
coming that's the plan.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.310
Want a scale?

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:28.340
Yeah!

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:30.760
Muromi-san.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.930
I haven't seen the mermaid since then.

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:40.900
That scale...

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:43.330
Huh? You know a mermaid?

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.110
Yeah, she's my friend.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:47.650
What's that?

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:48.530
Rock salt.

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:51.190
What was the mermaid like?

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.530
She had scallops on her head,

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:55.460
and she spoke kind of funny.

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:56.690
Her hair looked like this.

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:57.870
It's Muromi-san.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.720
Why do you want to see her?

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.390
I wanted to give her

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:03.670
my collection as thanks 
for giving me her scale.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.190
Take a look. The shells 
are pretty, aren't they?

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:07.000
Yeah.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:10.640
I think you can see Muromi-san 
if you head to Japan.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:13.170
Harpy might be able to take you there.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:16.500
But I'd kind of feel bad for 
Muromi-san if she did.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.790
Oh, a mermaid!

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:21.810
It is.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:23.270
Water...

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.030
I have coconuts.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:29.760
I don't have anything 
to cut them open.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:30.640
Give it over.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:32.790
Here.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.250
You want to see Muromi-san?

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.560
Hold on a second. I'll try calling her.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.720
Hello, Muromi-san?

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.110
She looks awful.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:53.790
<b>Huh, Yeti?</b>

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:53.790
<b>Her eyes are puffy!</b>

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:55.200
Isn't it worse to say

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.420
mean things to someone 
when they feel bad?

00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:00.900
But by overcoming this awful feeling,

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:03.900
we can feel like we're truly living.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.610
Hey, Mermaid-san.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:08.240
This is something precious to me...

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:11.720
<b>Houergh...</b>

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:17.370
<b>Bleaurgh...</b>

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:13.810
Stop it. You're going to make me—

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:15.870
I guess the mermaid isn't 
feeling well again today.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.370
I guess it was a bad day.

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:17.080
<b>Again?</b>

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:18.690
Hey, take this.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:20.460
I'll give you one, too.

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:23.700
Let's meet again sometime.

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:24.590
Sure.

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:29.340
Harpy, I'm back.

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:31.610
Harpy! Salt, salt!

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:32.800
I got this for you.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:36.990
Salt, salt.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.780
What's that? What?

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:42.120
Something precious.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.400
Muromi-san.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:56.310
<b>What's this?</b>

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:05.270
<i>Thanks for that.</i>

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:06.440
<i>If I'd been found any later,</i>

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:09.660
<i>I would've been a mammoth frozen
forever in the permafrost.</i>

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:12.550
<i>I need to thank you somehow.</i>

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:15.610
<i>I'll give you a scale.</i>

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:16.850
<i>Are you sure?</i>

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:20.060
<i>It's proof of our friendship.</i>

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.530
<i>We're friends.</i>

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:23.770
<i>Keep it for memories.</i>

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:27.690
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:30.660
<i>Actually, we don't know 
each other's names, do we?</i>

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:31.870
<i>I'm Muromi.</i>

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:32.780
<i>Who're you?</i>

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:34.460
<i>Yeti.</i>

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:35.740
<i>Yeti?</i>

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.170
<i>Sounds like a type of tea 
I have back at home.</i>

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:44.920
Muromi-san!

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:48.880
Watching the house, watching the house.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:52.860
<i>I'm going to deliver something 
to a village nearby.</i>

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:54.600
<i>Make sure you watch the house.</i>

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:55.930
<i>Got it, got it.</i>

00:08:58.320 --> 00:08:59.740
<b>Gurgle</b>

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.060
I'm hungry.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:10.440
That's quite the statue of Ganesha.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:13.660
It's not much, but please take this.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:14.900
Thank you, as always.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:17.520
Oh, it's Yeti-sama.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:18.800
Running errands?

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:23.490
<i>Oh yeah. I don't think there was
 any food left at home.</i>

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.830
<i>Harpy might be hungry.</i>

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:28.040
I'm back.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:31.000
Harpy, I'll make some food right now.

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:37.930
No, Harpy!

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:43.460
Why?

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:45.820
I was hungry.

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:46.710
Watching the house.

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:47.430
No food.

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:48.610
I couldn't leave.

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:00.590
Huh? Hello?

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:04.860
You're Yeti?

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:06.080
What is this? A hologram?

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:08.310
Sorry for calling so late.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:11.720
But, I didn't know what to do.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:13.300
<i>Wh-What's wrong?</i>

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:16.870
<i>I see...</i>

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:19.930
She gave it to me saying 
we were friends.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.890
Muromi-san is going 
to hate me for this.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.450
No, I don't think that'll happen.

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:27.640
I know Muromi-san. You've 
got nothing to worry about.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:28.870
It'll be fine.

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:30.190
<i>Are you sure?</i>

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:32.800
Yeah. Anyway, good night.

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:33.360
<i>Wai—</i>

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:46.900
I couldn't sleep very much.

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:48.620
Hi, hi!

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:49.890
Yechi!

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:52.330
Love, love! Kiss, kiss!

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:54.480
Muromi-san, why are you here?

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:56.740
You called Takkun last night, right?

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:57.420
Huh?

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:05.060
I was so happy my scale 
meant so much to you!

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.720
Who could hate Yetchi 
when she's so cute?

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.440
Harpy wants in, too!

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:14.330
Yeti!

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:16.500
Love, love! Kiss, kiss!

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:18.150
Hey, Yetchi's mine!

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:21.590
Love, kiss! Love, kiss!

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:26.540
<i>Um...</i>

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:27.750
Y-Yeah?

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.210
<i>Thanks for the other day.</i>

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:34.790
Please don't use this function 
when I'm in school.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:36.750
Muromi...

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:42.450
Uh...

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:49.680
That doesn't mean you can 
use it when I'm not in school.

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:53.100
"Like a rolling stone" 
rolling down a hill,

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.180
Otohime's life is headed straight down.

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:57.090
Ciel's going to read the 
preview this week, too?!

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:58.870
The once glorious Ryuuguujou has 
ceased to be,

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:00.040
popped much like a "bubble,"

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:01.850
and Otohime, who used to be at the top,

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:05.190
Next Time
Muromi-san and the Chill

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:03.270
finds herself plummeting to the bottom.

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:04.990
Now, due to the aftermath of Lehman Brothe—
